2025-05-26 11:18:40,314 - agentpress - DEBUG - api.py:666 - [DEBUG] Received response from agent_gen: {'message_id': 'b6ff951f-8c57-4f1e-aec1-9dbf65160bbd', 'thread_id': 'bba32dcb-93dc-4404-95d4-7b06a48f90fb', 'type': 'tool', 'is_llm_message': True, 'content': '{"role": "user", "content": "<tool_result> <scrape-webpage> ToolResult(success=True, output=\'[\\\\n  {\\\\n    \\"Title\\": \\"Digital payments in China - statistics & facts | Statista\\",\\\\n    \\"URL\\": \\"https://www.statista.com/topics/1211/digital-payments-in-china/\\",\\\\n    \\"Text\\": \\"[Skip to main content](https://www.statista.com/topics/1211/digital-payments-in-china/#main-content)\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n# Digital payments in China - statistics & facts\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nRegion\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nChina\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nChina\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nChoose a region:\\\\\\\\n![China](https://cdn.statcdn.com/static/icons/flag/iso/svg_flags/CN.svg)\\\\\\\\nChina\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nWhile many countries still struggled to promote mobile payments in response to the COVID-19 pandemic, China was already leading the rest of the world in building up a cashless society. The country was leading in user numbers and penetration rates and more than half of the Chinese population uses mobile payments each quarter. Over the years, Alipay and WeChat Pay have ruled the online payment market in China. The country\\\\\'s vibrant FinTech industry also brought about a flourishing e-commerce sector.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n## From cities to villages\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nDigital payments have not only been accepted by the tech-savvy middle-class from big cities. It has also changed the lives of rural residents and small business owners. In 2020, more than 20 percent of [Chinese mobile payment users](https://www.statista.com/statistics/1147688/china-city-distribution-of-mobile-payment-users/) were from counties, townships, and villages. The availability of mobile payments gives many people in rural areas access to financial services who had previously been outside the reach of traditional banking infrastructure. It has changed the lives of many rural residents and opened access to new income sources.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nThrough mobile payments and [e-commerce platforms](https://www.statista.com/statistics/1134335/china-most-valuable-ecommerce-companies/), rural residents not only have access to a broader range of products but also have new sales channels for their locally produced goods. Despite China\\\\\\\\u2019s economic and social development, many villages are still very remote and lag behind in living standards and infrastructure development. Via online retail, people can buy many articles that were previously hard to come by. Popular items include [clothes and footwear, as well as daily necessities.](https://www.statista.com/statistics/1228020/china-online-retail-sales-distribution-in-rural-area-by-category/) At the same time, villagers have utilized China\\\\\\\\u2019s large e-commerce platforms to market their locally produced products directly to consumers all over the country.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n## Face, Palm, and Finger: The User Becomes the Wallet\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nIn many countries, mobile payments use NFC technology in the smartphone or the smart wearable, both of which are linked to a bank or credit card. In China, however, payments are handled by a third-party service, such as [Alipay](https://www.statista.com/topics/12196/alipay/#topicOverview) or WeChat. The preferred method for identifying the other party in order to send or request payments was the QR or bar code. The provider in the background would then process the transaction.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nAfter QR codes, facial recognition and palm scans are the latest mobile payment methods in China. Many shopping malls, restaurants, and public transport systems offer these payment methods. Proponents claim that these methods are not only more convenient since they don\\\\\\\\u2019t require any device. In addition, they would also enhance security, which is one of the [leading concerns of Chinese mobile payment users](https://www.statista.com/statistics/1244342/china-top-necessary-improvements-of-mobile-payments/). Despite these claims of enhanced convenience and security, face and palm identification also bring about significant privacy risks that providers have to address.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nThis text provides general information. Statista assumes no\\\\\\\\nliability for the information given being complete or correct.\\\\\\\\nDue to varying update cycles, statistics can display more up-to-date\\\\\\\\ndata than referenced in the text.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nShow more\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\- Description\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nPublished by\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n[Daniel Slotta](https://www.statista.com/aboutus/our-research-commitment/2606/daniel-slotta)\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n,\\\\\\\\nJun 14, 2024\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nSubscribe\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nGet notified via email when statistics on this topic are updated.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n[Learn more about statistics updates via email](https://www.statista.com/getting-started/personalization-receiving-statistic-updates-via-email)\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n[Share on Twitter](https://twitter.com/intent/tweet?text=Digital%20payments%20in%20China%20-%20statistics%20%26%20facts%20https%3A%2F%2Fwww.statista.com%2Ftopics%2F1211%2Fdigital-payments-in-china%2F)[Share on LinkedIn](https://www.linkedin.com/sharing/share-offsite/?url=https://www.statista.com/topics/1211/digital-payments-in-china/?latest)[Share on Facebook](https://www.facebook.com/sharer.php?u=https://www.statista.com/topics/1211/digital-payments-in-china/)\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n## Key insights\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nNumber of online shoppers\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n[974m](https://www.statista.com/statistics/277391/number-of-online-buyers-in-china/)\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n![Number of online shoppers in China from 2014 to 2024 (in millions)](https://cdn.statcdn.com/Statistic/275000/277391-blank-100.png)\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nDetailed statistics\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nNumber of online shoppers in China 2014-2024\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n![Number of online shoppers in China from 2014 to 2024 (in millions)](https://cdn.statcdn.com/Statistic/275000/277391-blank-100.png)\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nDetailed statistics\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nNumber of online shoppers in China 2014-2024\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nNumber of online payment users\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n[904m](https://www.statista.com/statistics/248900/number-of-online-payment-users-in-china/)\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n![Number of online payment users in China from 2011 to 1st half of 2022 (in millions)](https://cdn.statcdn.com/Statistic/245000/248900-blank-100.png)\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nDetailed statistics\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nNumber of online payment users in China 2011-2022\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n![Number of online payment users in China from 2011 to 1st half of 2022 (in millions)](https://cdn.statcdn.com/Statistic/245000/248900-blank-100.png)\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nDetailed statistics\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nNumber of online payment users in China 2011-2022\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nPenetration rate of online payment\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n[92.8%](https://www.statista.com/statistics/248962/penetration-rate-of-online-payment-in-china/)\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n![Penetration rate of online payment in China from 2014 to 2024](https://cdn.statcdn.com/Statistic/245000/248962-blank-100.png)\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nDetailed statistics\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nPenetration rate of online payment in China 2014-2024\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n![Penetration rate of online payment in China from 2014 to 2024](https://cdn.statcdn.com/Statistic/245000/248962-blank-100.png)\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nDetailed statistics\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nPenetration rate of online payment in China 2014-2024\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n[Get more insights](https://www.statista.com/topics/1211/digital-payments-in-china/#topicInsights)\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n## Editor\\\\\\\\u2019s Picks       Editor\\\\\\\\u2019s Picks      Current statistics on this topic\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n[![Annual transaction value of mobile payments in China from 2013 to 2023 (in trillion yuan)](https://cdn.statcdn.com/Statistic/1060000/1060702-blank-100.png)\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nPayments\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nMobile payment transaction value in China 2013-2023](https://www.statista.com/statistics/1060702/china-mobile-payment-transaction-value/)\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n[![Penetration rate of online payment in China from 2014 to 2024](https://cdn.statcdn.com/Statistic/245000/248962-blank-100.png)\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nDemographics & Use\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nPenetration rate of online payment in China 2014-2024](https://www.statista.com/statistics/248962/penetration-rate-of-online-payment-in-china/)\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n[![Number of online payment users in China from 2011 to 1st half of 2022 (in millions)](https://cdn.statcdn.com/Statistic/245000/248900-blank-100.png)\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nPayments\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nNumber of online payment users in China 2011-2022](https://www.statista.com/statistics/248900/number-of-online-payment-users-in-china/)\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n## Recommended statistics\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n### General overview\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n4\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n- [Premium Statistic\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nNumber of internet users in China 2005-2024](https://www.statista.com/statistics/265140/number-of-internet-users-in-china/)\\\\\\\\n- [Premium Statistic\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\